.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-STATE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-state
.Nd declare system state, and converge the machine to it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm show | diff | health | history
.Nm
.Cm get Ar key
.Nm
.Cm set Ar key Ar value
.Nm
.Cm apply Op Fl -dry-run
.Nm
.Cm rollback Op Ar generation
.Nm
.Cm boot Op Fl -early
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /etc/novi/system.conf
is the declared state of this machine.
.Nm
reads that file, observes what the running system is actually doing,
and changes the system until the two agree.
Nothing caches the observation: service state comes from
s6-rc(1) ,
the hostname from
.Pa /proc/sys/kernel/hostname ,
and so on, so
.Cm diff
reports the machine rather than a record of it.
.Pp
The file is meant to be edited by hand.
.Cm set
rewrites one value in place, preserving comments and ordering, so a
file edited in an editor and a file edited through Settings are the
same document.
See
.Xr system.conf 5
for the keys.
.Pp
Declaring a value does not apply it.
.Cm set
changes the document;
.Cm apply
changes the machine.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "rollback [generation]"
.It Cm show
Print the declared state.
.It Cm get Ar key
Print one declared value.
.It Cm set Ar key Ar value
Declare a value.
Requires root.
.It Cm diff
Print declared against actual, one line per key that differs.
Exits 1 if anything has drifted.
.It Cm health
Report supervised services that are not working:
.Sy DOWN ,
.Sy CRASHLOOP
(has died and has been up under a minute), or
.Sy NOTREADY
(up over a minute without signalling the readiness it declares).
Exits 1 if any service is failing.
This is a different question from
.Cm diff :
a crash-looping service matches the document, because it is declared
on and the supervisor is keeping it up.
.It Cm apply Op Fl -dry-run
Converge the machine to the document.
With
.Fl -dry-run ,
print what would change and change nothing.
Requires root.
.It Cm history
List saved generations, newest last.
.It Cm rollback Op Ar generation
Restore a generation and apply it.
With no argument, the previous one.
Requires root.
.It Cm boot Op Fl -early
Converge at boot.
Called from
.Pa /etc/s6-linux-init/scripts/rc.init ;
not normally run by hand.
It always exits 0.
.Fl -early
converges only the keys that must precede services, which today is the
firewall.
.El
.Ss Generations
.Cm apply
saves what it observed
.Em before
it changed anything, under
.Pa /var/lib/novi-state/generations .
A generation is therefore the state the machine was in, not a copy of
the document that replaced it, which is what makes
.Cm rollback
able to undo an apply.
.Ss Keys that cannot drift
Some keys are read when they are used rather than held by anything:
.Va power.blank ,
.Va power.lid ,
.Va power.button ,
.Va storage.automount ,
and the
.Va agent.*
keys.
Nothing converges them, so
.Cm apply
has nothing to do for them and an unusable value is reported by
.Cm diff
as
.Sy unsupported
rather than being rejected when it is set.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/lib/novi-state/generations" -compact
.It Pa /etc/novi/system.conf
The declared state.
See
.Xr system.conf 5 .
.It Pa /var/lib/novi-state/generations
Saved generations.
.It Pa /etc/shadow
Password hashes.
Deliberately not part of the declared state:
.Pa system.conf
is world-readable and is meant to be committed to version control.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Cm diff
exits 1 when the machine has drifted from the document, and
.Cm health
exits 1 when a supervised service is failing.
Neither is an error.
.Cm boot
always exits 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Declare a hostname and a static address, then apply both:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-state set hostname workshop
# novi-state set network.address 192.168.1.50/24
# novi-state set network.gateway 192.168.1.1
# novi-state apply
.Ed
.Pp
See what has drifted without changing anything:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ novi-state diff
.Ed
.Pp
Undo the last apply:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-state rollback
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
A key this build does not recognise is reported as
.Sy unmanaged
rather than refused, so that a document written for a newer Novi still
applies on an older one.
A typo therefore reads as a line that does nothing;
.Cm diff
is where it shows up.
.Pp
One key that cannot converge does not stop the rest.
.Cm apply
reports it and continues, and exits non-zero at the end.
.Sh RECOVERY
Add
.Ar novi.state=off
to the kernel command line to skip boot convergence entirely, for when
the declared state is what is wrong with the machine.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-agent 1 ,
.Xr novi-wifi 1 ,
.Xr pkg 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5 ,
.Xr novi-slot 8
.Sh STANDARDS
The design is described in RFC 0002,
.Pa /usr/share/doc/novi/rfcs/0002-declarative-system-state.md .
